WEBVTT

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.270
I'm back to the world of people... of humans.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.290
You did it!

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:17.730
He did it!

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.450
He totally did it, damn it!

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.610
You kicked butt!  Amazing!

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.110
Stop spacing out.  Get to the hanger.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:28.560
You're in the way.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.580
Or do you want us to go around you?

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.480
You think you're a hero?  Give me a break.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:40.730
Yeah.  You just freaked out on the rear lines and then fired a big gun.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:46.110
What a hero!  All you did was pull the trigger.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.130
They're barely still flying and they can still talk like that.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.850
Pretty impressive.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.360
Well, you're still the hero today.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.400
No, I'm not.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.260
They're right.

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:03.540
I...

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.000
<b>Premonition</b>

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:42.240
Cheers to our new hero!

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.720
Cheers!

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.810
To the Shiranui Mk. 2!

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:48.300
- No, don't forget the Type 99 Cannon!

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:52.680
- And then Yuuya was like "Let's go, monsters!"

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.680
And he blew up all the BETA in a single blast!

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.240
Wow!

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:15.910
Yuuya!

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.330
What are you doing back here?

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:22.590
We can't have a victory party without the star!

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.750
The star of the party's the free liquor the USSR's providing.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:31.540
It's keeping them plenty entertained.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.820
No, that's thanks to you too hero!

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.500
Can it.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.020
I just decided when to pull the trigger.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.180
Yuuya.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:44.700
I'm not the hero here.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.760
It's the Lieutenant, who was brave enough to bring a top-secret weapon into Soviet territory.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:50.140
No, that's not true.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:53.640
Only you could've pulled off that shot.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.020
Perfect timing and target selection.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:03.130
Your skill and experience brought us the best result we could hope for.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:09.320
What's wrong?  Humility isn't like you.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:11.930
Lieutenant.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.320
Let me do the next one without that railgun.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:19.850
I want to move up the close-range melee combat test.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.570
What's brought this on?

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:28.000
I know the primary goal of this exercise is to test the Type 99 Cannon.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:34.110
But to make the Shiranui into the perfect TSF, I need real close-range experience.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:39.100
If the BETA show up when the Type 99 is undergoing maintenance,

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:42.000
we can just do one of the planned melee tests then.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.310
Changing the test schedule isn't easy, Mr. Hero.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:47.370
What's your hurry?

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.150
Do we know we'll get another chance?

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.120
Nobody knows when the BETA will appear.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:54.090
Please.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.730
Otherwise we'll waste this chance.

00:04:57.670 --> 00:04:59.300
Get a hold of yourself.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:03.170
It's a test pilot's job to do what his superiors ask of him.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:05.780
It's not your decision to make.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:10.220
My mission is to make the 94 Second the best it can be.

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:13.300
I need... the Shiranui needs real combat experience!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.250
I felt something for a single instant when I fought the Lieutenant's Type 00.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.050
Something I've never felt before.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:26.260
The Shiranui moved just how it wanted to, like I was moving my own body.

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.660
The only way to get that feeling back is real combat.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:34.780
I can only find it when my life is on the line and I'm pushed to the limit.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.200
That's how it feels to me.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.750
Bridges...

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.400
So please, Lieutenant!

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:43.890
The next time the BETA surface, give me a chance.

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:50.970
If I'm going to make this into Japan's new TSF, I... I have to change!

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:56.050
If I don't get that chance, and the Shiranui becomes a "good-enough" machine,

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.630
and because of that many Eishi die,

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.460
I couldn't take that!

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:08.190
I understand your request and your passion.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.060
Then...

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:13.340
To tell you the truth, it will be very difficult to change the schedule.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:17.480
But given that it's a request from the main test pilot,

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.170
I'll do what I can.

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:22.100
That's more than enough.  Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:25.470
As a reward for your efforts in battle

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:27.730
you'll be allowed 36 hours on standby in the base, starting tomorrow.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.630
Rest up for the next fight.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:36.620
I can't believe Yuuya actually bowed to someone.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.900
Was it this that changed him?  Or...

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:50.190
But your kindness backfired, Princess Yui.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.030
Damn it.

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.600
I'm stuck on standby in the base.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.510
I'm on the front lines, and I'm wasting time.

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.230
Looks like you're taking it easy.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.320
Is that how a hero gets to act?

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:11.960
Commander.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:17.220
Thanks to you, we were able to enjoy some quality vodka last night.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:21.130
I wanted to thank you, hero.

00:07:22.610 --> 00:07:25.420
I didn't do anything for you to thank me.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.200
Very humble.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:32.680
But over three thousand kills in your first sortie is probably a world record.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.200
You should be proud of it.

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:39.360
It's all my battalion's talking about right now.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:44.480
I'm honored you came all this way for some sarcastic remarks.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:48.030
And I'm glad that attitude has spread throughout your whole battalion.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.320
I'll tell you something as thanks for the vodka.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.990
You're a brave Eishi.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:01.520
But that immaturity of yours is clouding your eyes from the bigger picture.

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:03.710
The bigger picture?

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:07.980
In the end, people like that can't fight their own battles.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.990
Know your place, hero.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:14.720
If you don't want to get a lot of people killed for nothing.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:19.900
Wait, Commander!

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.250
I've said my thanks, hero.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:24.520
Stop calling me that.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.890
I know better than anybody that I'm no hero.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:34.260
You're damn right.  I don't see the big picture.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:37.680
But what about you?

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.190
That fight yesterday...

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:46.070
If you'd been able to help the mechanized infantry sooner,

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:48.440
I never would've had to be a hero!

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:55.540
I don't know what caused the delay, but how's that different from not seeing the big picture?

00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:58.380
It's not a bit different at all.

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:00.970
You're agreeing with me?

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:04.880
What are you fighting against?

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:09.470
When you blame something outside yourself for your own failure to do something,

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:11.600
the only thing you can convince is your own heart.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:13.400
You can never convince anyone else.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:20.630
If everyone around you seems convinced, it's proof they're spoiling you.

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:24.380
People like that are never good to have around.  Cut off ties with them immediately.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:26.880
What are you talking about?

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:30.800
If you can't take it all, decide what you're going to abandon.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:33.880
That's what your fight is, kid.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:37.790
I understand perfectly.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:40.430
Because you're like that,

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:43.320
because sacrificing your own allies means nothing to you,

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:50.180
your men have no problem doing something like that to citzens of your own country.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:56.790
Those girls are with the Central Strategic Research Corps, a group of privileged Russians.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.210
They're as elite as you can get.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:01.520
They are?

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:09.120
And most of the ones fighting on the front lines are citizens of conquered nations.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:14.490
You know they can't be happy about Russian elites walking around the base like they own the place.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.010
What?

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:21.470
America doesn't have any racial or class discrimination?

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:24.050
I see.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.050
It must be a nice place to live.

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:36.970
Are you one of those conquered peoples too?

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:38.060
No.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:41.980
I'm a Russian.

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:43.100
Commander!

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:47.830
Bye.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.880
What were you talking about with him?

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.950
Nothing important.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:11.420
Why is that man so important to you?

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:13.580
What does he have?

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:16.720
All of the men are uneasy.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:19.850
They want to know why you care about that coward.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:21.030
Lieutenant Ivanova.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:25.030
Please, Commander.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.340
He's an outsider.

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:28.870
He has nothing to do with us.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:33.200
I... our family...

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:33.960
Tasha.

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:37.040
Come here, Tasha.

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.790
Please don't go, Commander.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:45.030
Don't leave us!

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:47.200
It's okay, Tasha.

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:49.750
I belong to all of you.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:52.310
Really?  Really, Commander?

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.010
Yes.

00:11:54.010 --> 00:11:55.250
Really.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:12.540
<b>Imperial Ministry of Technology</b>

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:24.150
As you can see, the first test firing of the Prototype Type 99 EM Radiation Cannon is a success.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:25.670
What power.

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:29.390
With that the BETA are ours!

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.130
We could even retake Sadogashima!

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:39.720
But what if the Empire's secrets were somehow stolen, Iwaya-kun?

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:43.500
Taking a top-secret weapon to the Soviet Union...

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:47.450
Yui didn't ask for something easy.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:53.630
But if that was your decision, I'll do all I can do support it.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:58.090
I believe that you'll bring light to the empire's future...

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:13.180
If I'm going to make this into Japan's new TSF, I... I have to change!

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:22.190
In the end, did I bring one of the Empire's greatest secrets out here just to slow him down?

00:13:23.310 --> 00:13:26.000
I knew it would draw the Soviet's attention.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:28.070
But still...

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:34.030
Father, did I do the right thing?

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:39.500
Awesome.  Straight.

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:41.840
Seriously?  Damn it.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:45.210
They're back, right on schedule.

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:47.690
We can't sortie?

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:51.710
The BETA are here and we're the only ones who can't go?

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:55.240
Ensign Bridges, you were not given permission to speak.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:01.740
The Type 99 is offline.  We're not sure why.

00:14:01.740 --> 00:14:05.240
The main computer and all control systems are offline.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:10.090
It's not responding to any input and cannot be rebooted.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:16.670
The Imperial Diet has decided against dispatching any engineers who know the classified systems.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:20.990
So at the moment we're preparing to send encrypted data to the homeland...

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:24.740
In other words, we don't know when it'll be back online?

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:28.260
Yes, unfortunately.

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:34.600
If we can't test the Type 99, why not perform one of the other planned tests early?

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.970
Melee combat, perhaps?

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:41.140
We can't get the TSF retuned in time.

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:45.010
We're taking it back from the Type 99 loadout to the standard loadout.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:52.020
Then I'm sure my company would at least like to test the Active's melee abilities.

00:14:53.770 --> 00:15:00.340
Even with the 94 Second offline, I believe there's no problem with testing the remaining TSFs.

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:01.610
What do you think?

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.670
Indeed, there's no problem, but...

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:07.060
Hey, wait.

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:08.070
Yuuya!

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:09.190
Bridges!

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:11.030
How many times do I have to repeat myself?

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:16.890
Then why not have the 94 Second follow as a chaser?

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:23.280
Indeed, it would be good to have the same number of units accompanying as doing the exercise.

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:25.020
Get the 94 Second ready...

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:25.990
Wait a minute.

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.200
I told you the 94 Second was being tuned.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:32.980
There's no guarantee the BETA will continue to land in the appropriate numbers.

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:35.520
I think having him at least out there on the battlefield

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:40.200
would be good for Ensign Bridges, as well as the development process as a whole.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:44.370
Indeed, if it's simply accompanying them, it doesn't need a new loadout.

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.170
What do you think about that?

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:49.670
You may take this as my company's opinion on the matter.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:53.840
That's right.  If I can sortie, no matter what the reason is...

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.770
Once the fight starts I'll have my chance.

00:15:55.770 --> 00:16:01.380
Understood.  If you insist, I'll have the 94 Second sortie as a chaser.

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:05.420
However, I will pilot it this time.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:12.280
I don't understand this.

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:17.670
So you do not wish for Ensign Bridges to sortie, no matter what?

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:22.610
Is that because I have no combat experience?

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.630
I don't get it.

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:28.170
Manandal!

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.320
It's alright.

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:30.560
Continue, Ensign.

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:32.700
You're too overprotective.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:35.980
Stop talking and let him do what he wants.

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:38.300
Eishi can only grow on a real battlefield.

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:41.640
Tell us what you really think, princess.

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:45.310
You want to get him some real combat experience too, right?

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.750
Then I'll pilot the 94 Second as a Chaser.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:53.440
Yuuya can go in the Active.  Then there's no problem.

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:55.240
Chobi, you...

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:58.920
Don't worry.  I'll protect Yuuya!

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:05.810
I don't know if she can do it on her own, so I'll go as backup.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:08.000
What do you mean you don't know?

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:10.250
So what will you do?

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:13.630
You heard what your comrades said.

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:14.990
What will you do?

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:15.750
Comrades?

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:25.220
If you can't take it all, decide what you're going to abandon.

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:28.350
That's what your fight is, kid.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:32.350
So that's it, Commander?

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:38.660
Alright.  I'll leave the 94 Second to Lt. Takamura.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:44.260
I'm happy you said that, but priority one for the plan

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:47.270
is to get close-range data for the 94 Second.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.260
Right, Lt.?

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:52.360
Ensign Bridges...

00:17:55.220 --> 00:18:01.450
Oh my, Ensign Bridges.  A test pilot shouldn't give up that easily.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:04.810
Every member Argos Test Flight will sortie.

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:08.310
Our goal is to get close-range data on the Active.

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:10.920
We will not change the pilots.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:14.730
This is my official request.  Please take care of it.

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:16.530
Listen...

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:18.020
Ensign Bridges.

00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:20.770
I know this may not be my place to speak,

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:23.350
but Mr. Heinemann is not making a request.

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:25.080
He's giving an order.

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:27.780
Is this acceptable to Lt. Dahl?

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:31.480
Yes.

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:38.580
Comrade Efremov!

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:40.010
Who is your father?

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:43.520
My great motherland, the Soviet Union!

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:45.090
Comrade Upenskona!

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:46.580
Who is your mother?

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:49.680
My beloved motherland, the land of Eurasia!

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:51.370
Comrade Kontarsky!

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:53.250
What is your task?

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:56.120
To slay my hated foe, the BETA!

00:18:56.490 --> 00:19:00.780
As a Russian, I am not worthy to earn your trust.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:04.200
Comrade Baranova, who fights with you?

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:07.590
My trusted companions, the Zhar Battalion!

00:19:07.590 --> 00:19:14.660
But even so, I will to stand on the battlefield with you, and continue to train you.

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:17.620
To ensure as many children survive as I can...

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:20.990
Valiant Eishi of the Zhar Battalion!

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:23.800
We are a single sword forged in the fires of hell!

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.960
Just like your mothers want...

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:29.370
Stand and take up your weapons!

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.840
Cowardice and hesitation are treason!

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:34.530
The fate of the motherland rests in our hands.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:36.820
- Destroy these invaders in the name of the Zhar Battalion,

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:39.550
- I too hope that somone out there

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.540
- and fight till your last breath!

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:44.250
is training my child to keep death away.

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:47.770
Mom!  Mom!

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:51.110
Nash Ura!

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:52.820
Nash Ura!

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:54.120
Nash Ura!

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:55.370
Nash Ura!

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:57.630
Please, forgive me.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:02.290
Please forgive me for only being able to fight for such a selfish reason...

00:20:22.980 --> 00:20:23.720
Look!

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:26.120
They're like spilled Borscht!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.480
Don't eat it all.

00:20:27.480 --> 00:20:29.040
We need to save some for our guests.

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:31.150
Come on, squiddy!

00:20:31.150 --> 00:20:32.900
Die!

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:35.410
Hey, hero.

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:37.180
You just going to stand there again today?

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:41.470
Idar Test Flight has finished their tests.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.290
Standing by in the combat area.

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:47.540
Argos Test Flight has finished 65% of their assigned tests.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:52.570
In the end, I had to send him out onto the battlefield in an incomplete TSF.

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.560
What was it I was trying to protect so badly

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:59.860
that I took out an Imperial Secret and ruined an Eishi's pride?

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:03.850
That's more than enough.  Thank you, Lieutenant.

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:06.860
All this was my choice.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:08.350
My responsibility.

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:09.730
Lt. Takamura.

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:13.410
As you can see the battle is moving in our favor.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:16.070
There's no need for the both of us to be here.

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:20.650
Why don't you go do your job?

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:21.550
While you have the chance.

00:21:22.910 --> 00:21:23.790
But...

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:28.260
Leave to others what you can, and then do the things only you can do.

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:31.250
Don't you think that's how a commanding officer should act?

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:33.020
Lt. Ibrahim?

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:35.870
I'll go to Hanger 16.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:37.380
Take care of the Test Flight for me.

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:49.070
That was easier than I thought.

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:52.410
These are the survivors of the group that landed last time.

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:53.450
That's how it always is.

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:56.440
I've confirmed that the number of enemies is dropping.

00:21:56.440 --> 00:21:59.000
It'll only be an hour or so to clean up the rest of them.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.900
I want this over with.

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:02.980
I'd like to get back to our game.

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:05.730
What, you want to lose the clothes on your back?

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:06.780
What?

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:10.550
What's this?

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:12.120
Multiple moving epicenters.

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:14.040
Epicenter depth raising rapidly?

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:15.380
Identify the waveform!

00:22:15.380 --> 00:22:17.030
Impossible...  They're so close!

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:21.140
This vibration...

00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:22.110
Lt. Takamura!

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:24.460
We have a Code 991.

00:22:24.460 --> 00:22:25.970
A BETA attack from underground!

00:22:29.550 --> 00:22:31.890
An army corps sized group of BETA is approaching.

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:33.740
Coordinates confirmed.

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:36.830
13 km NW of the base?

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:10.070
Damn it!  Are the people at the base okay?

00:24:10.890 --> 00:24:13.820
You needn't worry about Lt. Takamura.

00:24:14.440 --> 00:24:17.420
Unfortunately, retreat is impossible.

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:24.310
<b>BETA Offensive</b>

00:24:17.740 --> 00:24:19.190
Ready yourself.

00:24:20.120 --> 00:24:22.570
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.570 --> 00:24:24.120
BETA Offensive
